=== Switching project
kind: flow
domain: Projects
doc: What the console loads when a person picks another project.
---
#> The person picks a project in the menu -> project_actions.switch_project
The menu lists the projects they have a role on.
#> The console loads the project -> GET /v1/projects/{project}
It asks for the project with its usage and the person's role, and at the same time for its instances and its disks. Any role is enough to look.
#> The API checks the person's role -> project_roles.authorize_project
Someone with no role on the project is told it does not exist.
#> The project is shown and remembered
The console shows the project, how much of its quota is left, and only the buttons the person's role allows. It remembers the project in the browser and opens it first next time.

=== Deleting a project
kind: flow
domain: Projects
doc: What stands between pressing "Delete project" and the project being gone.
---
#> The person presses Delete project -> project_actions.delete_project
If the console already knows they are not an admin, or that the project still holds instances or disks, it says so and stops. Otherwise it asks them to confirm, and warns that it cannot be undone.
#> The API checks again -> DELETE /v1/projects/{project}
The console's picture may be out of date, so the API makes its own checks. Only an admin of the project may delete it.
#> A project that holds anything is refused -> projects.delete_project
The project must hold no instances and no disks. Boot disks count, so every instance has to be deleted first. The console tells the person to delete them and try again.
#> The project and its roles are removed -> project_store.project_delete
Everyone who had a role on it loses it.
#> The console opens another project -> session_actions.open_first_project
It reloads the person's projects and opens the first one, or the empty page if none are left.
